fibo-be-ge-usj:AmericanSamoaEntity a owl:NamedIndividual,
        fibo-be-ge-ge:RegionalSovereignty ;
    rdfs:label "American Samoa entity" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy fibo-be-ge-usj: ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <http://americansamoa.gov/>,
        <https://www.doi.gov/oia/islands/american-samoa> ;
    skos:definition "individual representing the unincorporated territory and polity of the United States located in the South Pacific Ocean, known as American Samoa" ;
    fibo-be-ge-ge:hasSharedSovereigntyOver lcc-3166-2-us:AmericanSamoa ;
    fibo-be-ge-ge:isRepresentedBy fibo-be-ge-usj:GovernmentOfAmericanSamoa ;
    cmns-av:explanatoryNote "American Samoa consists of five main islands and two coral atolls. The largest and most populous island is Tutuila, with the Manu'a Islands, Rose Atoll, and Swains Island also included in the territory. American Samoa is part of the Samoan Islands chain, located west of the Cook Islands, north of Tonga, and some 300 miles (500 km) south of Tokelau." .

